    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup construction prioritizes high-upside speed and situational advantages, led by **Seiya Suzuki** (67.36), **Corbin Carroll** (64.88), and **Brice Turang** (64.10). **Seiya Suzuki** is our strongest play, leveraging a favorable matchup against Lugo to maximize his base projection, while **Corbin Carroll** remains a core anchor despite the threat of Yamamoto\u2019s holding game limiting his stolen base potential. **Brice Turang** earns high marks for his leadoff spot and his ability to exploit the slow delivery of Bradley, which should provide a significant cushion for our pursuit of steals. Conversely, **Max Muncy** (62.89) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (60.58) benefit immensely from wind-aided conditions, driving their scores into the \"Strong\" category despite challenging matchups against Bennett.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Cole Young** on the bench. His projection of 39.56 fell just shy of our 40.0 \"Zebras Floor,\" primarily due to a poor park factor and the efficiency risk posed by Griffin Jax. While **Cole Young** offers upside, the data suggests that starting him against such a formidable arm is an unnecessary risk when we are managing game caps. Elsewhere, we are closely monitoring the matchup for **Jose Caballero**, whose score (52.65) was suppressed by a difficult encounter with Sale; however, his unique ability to leverage platoon advantages keeps him in the mix. We remain in a holding pattern regarding our injured core\u2014**James Wood** and **Giancarlo Stanton**\u2014whose absence continues to constrain our depth, leaving us to lean heavily on the remaining active roster to carry the load in SB and AVG.",
